1275	    // audio or revoke its current blob URL here. Destroy fires on LV
1276	    // reconnect/re-mount (long phone sleep → server LV process times out
1277	    // → client re-mount on wake) — and the <audio> element survives
1278	    // (phx-update="ignore"). Pausing or revoking would interrupt the
1279	    // user's listening session at exactly the moment they wake the phone
1280	    // hoping playback continues. If the player is genuinely going away
1281	    // (user navigates off the reader), the <audio> element gets removed
1282	    // from the DOM, which auto-pauses it — no explicit pause needed.
1283	    //
1284	    // We do still abort and revoke the *prefetch* slot: that blob is not
1285	    // tied to the playing audio element, so leaking it across re-mount
1286	    // would just waste memory.
1287	    ctx.onDestroy(() => {
